M1 first-failure measurements, selfhost route vs image route (2026-10-24, JUN-31)
All producer runs: podman 5.6.0 --platform linux/amd64, python:3.12-alpine,
qemu-user binfmt, KEXE_SECCOMP=if-available KEXE_CAP_RESOURCES_35=/work.
Host: macOS 26.4 arm64. Python orchestrates and hashes only.

== 0. reference image (the route M1 must replace), reproduced byte-identically ==
$ podman .../python:3.12-alpine  # host side: shim-pinned amu (pin 74ca4aa68 +
  pe32plus pad 73b7ac475), bin/amu nbb route:
$ bin/amu compile boot-fixture.kotoba --target x86_64-aiueos-kernel-v1 \
    --artifact image --fuel 32768 --output KERNEL.ref-image.elf --jvm-free
exit 0  {:ok true, :artifact-bytes 110872, :fuel-metering :on,
         :target :x86_64-aiueos-kernel-v1}
sha256 e7ee95b9f8992b679af7dc10ba14eb0460ead81b508be05fdb6feb43b9b72212
  = the boot-jump run's KERNEL.ELF (aiueos-jun31-boot-jump-qemu43-20261024),
    byte-identical. The boot-proven artifact is exactly reproducible from
    os/aiueos/uefi/boot-fixture.kotoba (source sha256 018a939c...).

== 1. W1: the selfhost compiler refuses the IMAGE route (first failed element) ==
$ podman ... /work/S-x86_64.elf compile /work/boot-fixture.kotoba \
    --target x86_64-aiueos-kernel-v1 --artifact image --fuel 32768 \
    --output /work/KERNEL.selfhost.elf
exit 2
seed-x86_64-aiueos-object: E7100 expected compile SOURCE --target x86_64-aiueos-kernel-v1 --output NEW_OBJ [--fuel POSITIVE_BUDGET]

Producer: S-x86_64.elf (1,532,416 B, sha256 f74fd09b36332c13...) = the
loaderless selfhost fixed point's x86_64 static compiler
(selfhost-bootstrap.py, S1=S2=S3=root 8256bfd8..., rootReproduces true).
Its kernel-v1 driver is `seed-x86_64-aiueos-object`: the kernel OBJECT ABI
only. --artifact is not in its grammar at all. The selfhost closure carries
kotoba.native.elf64's package-kernel-OBJECT shape
(selfhost-unity.kotoba:13574) and no image packager.

== 2. W2: the fixture's boot-evidence ops are unexpressible in the object route ==
$ podman ... /work/S-x86_64.elf compile /work/boot-fixture.kotoba \
    --target x86_64-aiueos-kernel-v1 --output /work/KERNEL.obj-from-fixture.o \
    --fuel 32768
exit 1
seed-x86_64-linux: /work/boot-fixture.kotoba at 1120 detail 0 seed-x86_64-linux: E2101

Byte offset 1120 is exactly the head `(kernel-out-u8 233 66)` of the fixture's
two port writes. E2101 = the head is not in the seed library (selfhost-unity
E2101 refs: "a local in HEAD position is refused ... any other local in head
position: E2101" / "(typed-set-nth ...) at the head when the library is
missing").

Same refusal on the object route's own export profile (a `kotoba_aiueos_*`
variant of the same body):
$ podman ... /work/S-x86_64.elf compile /work/boot-fixture-obj.kotoba \
    --target x86_64-aiueos-kernel-v1 --output /work/boot-fixture-obj.o \
    --fuel 32768
exit 1
seed-x86_64-linux: /work/boot-fixture-obj.kotoba at 303 detail 0 ...: E2101
Byte offset 303 is the same head `(kernel-out-u8 233 66)`.

`kernel-out-u8` / `kernel-out-u32` (the contract's :boot evidence operations,
contracts/value-runtime-kernel-image-v1.edn) are emitted by kotoba-native's
native backend (src/kotoba/native/x86_64.cljk:2058 `(= op 'kernel-out-u8)
(emit-kernel-out args 8 env ctx)`, machine_ir.cljk:826 'kernel-out-u8 :out-u8)
— i.e. by the bin/amu route only. The selfhost seed emitter has no entry for
them.

== 3. reference layout (what the seed image route must emit) ==
KERNEL.ref-image.elf, 110,872 B (elf-facts-ref-image.txt):
  e_type=2 (ET_EXEC) e_machine=62 e_entry=0x101000 e_phnum=2
  ph[0] PT_LOAD RX poff=4096  vaddr=paddr=0x101000 filesz=memsz=144
  ph[1] PT_LOAD RW poff=32768 vaddr=paddr=0x108000 filesz=memsz=77824
  280 B tail: 24 B pad + 4 section headers at e_shoff=110616 (.text .data .shstrtab + null)
Every window clause passes (s0mem 144 <= 4096, s1mem 77,824, klen 110,872).

Emitter located (window-classification NOTES §1 "not located" gap closed):
kotoba-native src/kotoba/native/elf64.cljc.cljk package-kernel (1091-1182).
  - image-base 0x100000 (:20), text-offset page-size=4096 (:21)
    -> entry-address 0x101000; seg0 = entry-shim + code (shim 77 B non-live,
       :1116 boot-size (if live? live-boot-shim-size 77); 144-77 = 67 B of
       fixture code)
  - kernel-data-offset-for (:60-62) =
    max minimum-kernel-data-offset, page-align(text-offset + text-size)
    -> seg1 file offset is max(32768, page-align(4096+seg0size)), exactly the
       three-artifact observation of window-classification §1
  - kernel-runtime-data-size (:52) = kernel-stack-offset + kernel-stack-bytes
    -> seg1 memsz is the fixed 77,824 B context/sealed-fuel region
  - sections/headers assembled :1146-1161; tail 280 B is pad + 4 shdrs.
